  {"date": "1997-08-03", "venue": "Gorge Amphitheatre", "city": "George", "state": "WA", "gap": 2, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "> \"Dirt\", the version demonstrates considerable growth over a short period of time. Page's fills fall like scales between Fish's off-kilter percussion, the jam itself a revelation. Trey's riffing and soloing is forceful, with each musician acutely attuned and playing \"out\" as if a means to somehow reign their sound \"in\". Impressive.", "prev": "Dirt", "in": ">", "next": "My Mind's Got a Mind of its Own", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-08-11", "venue": "Deer Creek Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The band still toying with set placement, here, \"Vultures\" anchors the second set for the second time, and with great results.  While a true appraisal will only coincide with the arrival of a crisper AUD (or SBD!), what IS clear is that Trey has grown comfortable playing within the \"confines\" of the composition's compact form, his soloing crisp and rich with both discordant and melodic variation, and really impressive phrasing.", "out": ">", "prev": "Piper", "next": "My Soul", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-08-17", "venue": "Loring Commerce Centre", "city": "Limestone", "state": "ME", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "prev": "Dogs Stole Things", "next": "Water in the Sky", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1997-12-13", "venue": "Pepsi Arena", "city": "Albany", "state": "NY", "gap": 21, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Clearly comfortable, the band works through the intro into an awesome \"middle\" section featuring, unsurprisingly, inspired and deft play from Trey. The song loses its shape to assume a different form, the jam cooling after the 5:30 mark to become decidedly - and pleasantly - spacey, before a spirited return to the song's closing refrain.", "prev": "Sample in a Jar", "next": "Tube", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1998-07-29", "venue": "Riverport Amphitheater", "city": "Maryland Heights", "state": "MO", "gap": 28, "set": "1", "note": "Debut of new arrangement.", "prev": "Farmhouse", "in": ">", "next": "Glide", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1998-08-06", "venue": "Lakewood Amphitheatre", "city": "Atlanta", "state": "GA", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "prev": "Beauty of My Dreams", "next": "Train Song", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "1998-11-27", "venue": "Worcester Centrum Centre", "city": "Worcester", "state": "MA", "gap": 32, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Rearranged and redefined (see History), the band offers another strong version, at home in another strong first set. The band breaks again for more ambient play, moored by some serious Trey sustain which fades to cool into a swirling ambient pool. After passing through a passage of concerted \"noise\", Fish drives the band to a rocking conclusion.", "prev": "Dogs Stole Things", "next": "When the Circus Comes", "nb": 1},
